{
  "extends": "@tsconfig/strictest/tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "allowJs": true,
    "allowSyntheticDefaultImports": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "importHelpers": true,
    "inlineSourceMap": true,
    "inlineSources": true,
    "lib": [
      "DOM",
      "ESNext"
    ],
    "module": "node16",
    "moduleResolution": "node16",
    "noEmit": true,
    // `@tsconfig/strictest` sets this to `false`, and that setting earns its keep only where the `.d.ts`
    // files ARE the product -- which is the release branches, not here. This package ships no types; it
    // ships scripts. What `false` bought instead was a permanently red `tsc --noEmit` on somebody else's
    // declaration file: `eslint-import-context` is a CommonJS package whose `lib/types.d.ts` type-imports
    // the ESM-only `type-fest` with no `resolution-mode` attribute, which TypeScript 6 rejects as TS1541.
    // It arrives transitively under `eslint-import-resolver-typescript` / `eslint-plugin-import-x`,
    // nothing here imports it, and it is still unfixed in the package's latest version (0.2.0, checked
    // 2026-09-15), so there is no upgrade that clears it. There is no per-package escape hatch either --
    // `skipLibCheck` is all-or-nothing. The repo root's own `tsconfig.json` already made this same call
    // for the same reason. Our own `.ts` files are unaffected: `skipLibCheck` only skips declarations.
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "target": "ESNext",
    "types": [
      "node"
    ],
    "verbatimModuleSyntax": true
  },
  "include": [
    "./**/*.ts",
    "./eslint.config.mts"
  ]
}
